From 2f997caccb18a0bee9d4b5170f28de0ca87c8e49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Lane A <lane-a@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 15:11:38 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 06/18] feat(reframe): show the screen being reacted to,
 stacked over the reactor

Root cause #1b of clip1.mp4: the stimulus (the stage screen with the "Best IRL
Streamer" nominees) only appeared in wide shots, and framing either showed the
whole 16:9 frame small or cropped to a face and cut the screen away.

media/screen_subject.py, SCREEN_SUBJECT (default OFF until Luffy approves):
the clip is sampled every 1.5 s for a lit, coloured/detailed rectangle in the
upper half of the frame (a screen), with the faces not on it; runs of
sightings (gaps <= 4.5 s merged) become decisions: a readable-fit window when
screen + people fit in 80% of the width, otherwise the existing stacked split
layout with the whole screen in the top tile and the main person (largest
face off the screen) in the bottom tile. When a clip has screen runs, the
whole clip uses one full-frame fit layout and switches to the stack only while
the screen is on (the shot-by-shot subject plan switched 44 times in 60 s).
Phase-2 harness turns on all review switches.

Evidence: handoff/quality-clip1/step3/ - same 141-201 s window: 22.5-46.5 s is
the nominees screen on top (readable: "BEST IRL STREAMER", "EVELYN ORTIZ")
over the streamer watching (frame_30s_stack.png); before_vs_all_steps.mp4.
Limits: brightness heuristic; low-in-frame screens (phones) skipped; "main
person" = largest face; ~94 s analysis per 60 s of 4K.
Tests: test_screen_subject 8/8.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
